 -- easywall maintainers <12394156+jp1337@users.noreply.github.com>  Wed, 12 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000

easywall (2.5.0) unstable; urgency=high

  * Fix: the packaged core daemon could not talk to the web interface at all.
    CapabilityBoundingSet=CAP_NET_ADMIN leaves a root service without CAP_CHOWN
    and CAP_DAC_OVERRIDE, so the control socket stayed root:root and the web
    user was refused on connect, and /var/lib/easywall — owned by that user —
    was unreadable to the daemon, which never wrote rules.json. The unit now
    runs the daemon in the easywall group and the data directory is group
    writable; neither needs a wider capability set
  * Fix: a session cookie was accepted for thirty days rather than the
    documented ten minutes, and logging out therefore wore off — replaying the
    cookie once the revocation record had expired signed the visitor back in
  * Fix: the version was never compiled in. It was a constant, and the linker's
    -X silently does nothing to a constant, so every build reported the literal
    in the source whatever tag it came from. Both binaries now accept --version
  * Firewall rule ordering, per-source rate limiting, logging, the acceptance
    window, first-run wizard and Debian layout fixes — see CHANGELOG.md

 -- easywall maintainers <12394156+jp1337@users.noreply.github.com>  Tue, 11 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000

easywall (2.0.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Complete rewrite in Go (nftables via netlink, no Python dependency)
  * Two-process architecture: privileged core daemon + unprivileged web process
  * Direct nftables netlink API — no subprocess, no injection risk
  * Argon2id password hashing (replaces SHA512 with hostname salt)
  * Two-step activation with auto-rollback prevents SSH lockouts
  * Docker coexistence: own nftables table inet easywall
  * i18n: English and German
  * Light/Dark mode with OS preference detection
  * Export/Import rules as JSON
  * Auto-renewing self-signed TLS certificate
  * Debian package: only depends on nftables and openssl
  * logrotate config for audit log
  * CI: GitHub Actions, Dependabot, CodeQL, govulncheck

